 "host": "#specTable",
 "caption": "Resolution element and single-line centroid precision of 31 spectrograph modes at SNR = 100 per pixel. FWHM = λ<sub>ref</sub>/R unless quoted by the source (PFS); FWHM in km/s = c/R. σ<sub>rule</sub> = FWHM/(SNR·√N<sub>pix</sub>), N<sub>pix</sub> = pixels per FWHM; σ<sub>CRB</sub> = photon-noise Cramér–Rao bound for one unresolved Gaussian absorption line of depth 0.5, integrated over pixels (<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#ref-bouchy2001\">Bouchy et al. 2001</a>, eqs. 8–12, σ<sub>D</sub> = 0). For emission lines (peak 10⁴ e⁻/pixel, no background) the bound is ≈ 2.4× smaller than the rule. Both scale as λ/(R·SNR·√N<sub>pix</sub>): multiply by 100/SNR for other signal levels. <b>Photon noise only:</b> read noise, blends, intrinsic width and asymmetry, LSF mismatch, flat-field and pixel-size errors (HARPS floor ≈ 0.01 px = 0.15 mÅ, <a class=\"cite\" href=\"#ref-lovis2007\">Lovis &amp; Pepe 2007</a>) and wavelength-solution errors are excluded, so real per-line accuracies are worse. R conventions differ (design vs measured, e.g. HARPS 115 000 vs 110 000); DESI R is the mid-point of each quoted range; LAMOST-MRS and WEAVE samplings (3 px) are assumptions; UVES, HIRES and CRIRES+ samplings are slit-width/pixel-scale estimates and LAMOST-LRS is sampled on its 10⁻⁴-dex output grid (hover the basis column for each derivation). Verbatim source values: <code>data/curated/spectrograph_precision.csv</code>.",
